#: ../../../aliases.rst:302
msgid "Directory Stack"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../aliases.rst:306
msgid "``pushd``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../aliases.rst:307
msgid ""
"Adds a directory to the top of the directory stack, or rotates the stack, "
"making the new top of the stack the current working directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../aliases.rst:1
msgid ""
"usage: pushd [-h] [-n] [-q] [+N|-N|dir]\n"
"\n"
"Adds a directory to the top of the directory stack, or rotates the stack,\n"
"making the new top of the stack the current working directory.\n"
"\n"
"On Windows, if the path is a UNC path (begins with `\\\\<server>\\<share>`) "
"and if the `DisableUNCCheck` registry\n"
"value is not enabled, creates a temporary mapped drive letter and sets the "
"working directory there, emulating\n"
"behavior of `PUSHD` in `CMD.EXE`\n"
"\n"
"positional arguments:\n"
"  +N|-N|dir    * dir :\n"
"                   Makes dir be the top of the stack,\n"
"                   making it the new current directory as if it had been "
"supplied as an argument to the cd builtin.\n"
"               * +N :\n"
"                   Brings the Nth directory (counting from the left of the "
"list printed by dirs, starting with zero)\n"
"                   to the top of the list by rotating the stack.\n"
"               * -N :\n"
"                   Brings the Nth directory (counting from the right of the "
"list printed by dirs, starting with zero)\n"
"                   to the top of the list by rotating the stack.\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help   show this help message and exit\n"
"  -n, --cd     Suppresses the normal change of directory when adding "
"directories to the stack,\n"
"               so that only the stack is manipulated.\n"
"  -q, --quiet  Do not call dirs, regardless of $PUSHD_SILENT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../aliases.rst:314
msgid "``popd``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../aliases.rst:315
msgid "Removes entries from the directory stack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../aliases.rst:1
msgid ""
"usage: popd [-h] [-n] [-q] [+N|-N]\n"
"\n"
"When no arguments are given, popd removes the top directory from the stack\n"
"and performs a cd to the new top directory.\n"
"The elements are numbered from 0 starting at the first directory listed with "
"``dirs``;\n"
"that is, popd is equivalent to popd +0.\n"
"\n"
"positional arguments:\n"
"  +N|-N        Removes the Nth directory (counting from the left/right of "
"the list printed by dirs w.r.t. -/+ prefix),\n"
"               starting with zero.\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help   show this help message and exit\n"
"  -n, --cd     Suppresses the normal change of directory when removing "
"directories from the stack,\n"
"               so that only the stack is manipulated.\n"
"  -q, --quiet  Do not call dirs, regardless of $PUSHD_SILENT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../aliases.rst:321
msgid "``dirs``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../aliases.rst:322
msgid ""
"Displays the list of currently remembered directories.  Can also be used to "
"clear the directory stack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../aliases.rst:1
msgid ""
"usage: dirs [-h] [-c] [-p] [-v] [-l] [N]\n"
"\n"
"Manage the list of currently remembered directories.\n"
"\n"
"positional arguments:\n"
"  N           Displays the Nth directory (counting from the left/right "
"according to +/x prefix respectively),\n"
"              starting with zero\n"
"\n"
"options:\n"
"  -h, --help  show this help message and exit\n"
"  -c          Clears the directory stack by deleting all of the entries.\n"
"  -p          Print the directory stack with one entry per line.\n"
"  -v          Print the directory stack with one entry per line,\n"
"              prefixing each entry with its index in the stack.\n"
"  -l          Produces a longer listing; the default listing format\n"
"              uses a tilde to denote the home directory."
msgstr ""

